# Test: every method ze help ai --json publishes is one a handler registers
# VALIDATES: AC-5 and AC-10 of spec-rpc-published-name-does-not-reach-its-handler,
#            user story 1 -- the RPCs array the MCP tool ze_reference hands a
#            client carries the method each handler registers, and that method
#            carries the prefix of the subsystem that registers it
# PREVENTS: a method built from a module file name (ze-l2tp-api:summary, which
#           no handler answers) or a shared verb prefix (ze-show:) reaching an
#           agent, which then calls a name that resolves to nothing
# NOTE: Go regexp has no backreference, so a general "no method twice" check is
#       not expressible here. The reject below pins one method that YANG
#       documents and a builtin also registers, the case that published twice;
#       TestBuildPublishesEachRPCOnce (internal/component/aihelp) proves the
#       universal claim.
# NOTE: one command on purpose, because an expect matches the ACCUMULATED stdout
#       of every command in the file.

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze help ai --json
expect=exit:code=0

expect=stdout:contains="wire-method": "ze-l2tp:summary"
expect=stdout:contains="wire-method": "ze-bgp:rib-routes"
expect=stdout:contains="wire-method": "ze-plugin:system-command-help"
reject=stdout:pattern="wire-method": "ze-[a-z0-9-]+-api:
reject=stdout:pattern="wire-method": "ze-(show|set|clear|delete|generate|validate|monitor):
reject=stdout:contains="wire-method": "ze-system:
reject=stdout:contains="wire-method": "ze-rib:show"
reject=stdout:pattern=(?s)"wire-method": "ze-plugin:session-ready".*"wire-method": "ze-plugin:session-ready"
